    <bpmn:process id="W_W1205" name="W1205. PCI-DSS Compliance for POS Payment Card Data &amp; Annual QSA Audit Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual PCI-DSS compliance cycle; or triggered by significant change to payment processing environment (new POS system, new payment gateway, new network topology)
Frequency: Annual on-site QSA audit; quarterly network vulnerability scans; continuous compliance monitoring
Volume: 600 POS terminals across 200 stores processing ~36% card transactions (~1M card transactions/month)
Owner: IT Security Manager
Participants: IT Security Manager, CIO, POS System Vendor, Network Infrastructure Team, Payment Gateway Provider, QSA (Qualified Security Assessor), VP Legal
Source: workflow W1205 — PCI-DSS Compliance for POS Payment Card Data &amp; Annual QSA Audit Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1205_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1205_Lane1" name="IT Security Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1205_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1205_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1205_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1205_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1205_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1205_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1205_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1205_Lane2" name="QSA">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1205_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1205_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1205_Start4" name="Annual PCI-DSS compliance cycle; or triggered by significant change to payment processing…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1205_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1205_Task5" name="PCI-DSS scope definition">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: PCI-DSS scope definition: IT Security Manager defines PCI-DSS scope annually: (a) Cardholder Data Environment (CDE) includes: all 600 POS terminals, POS network segments, payment gateway integration servers, and any systems that store, process, or transmit cardholder data, (b) identifies segmentation boundaries between CDE and general corporate network, (c) documents data flow diagram showing how card data enters, traverses, and exits the environment
Responsible (R): IT Security Manager
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1205_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1205_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1205_Task6" name="Self-Assessment Questionnaire (SAQ)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Self-Assessment Questionnaire (SAQ): For locations not requiring on-site assessment: IT Security Manager completes PCI-DSS SAQ (SAQ D for BuildRight as a large merchant with 600 terminals): (a) 12 requirement categories covering network security, access control, encryption, vulnerability management, and security policies, (b) documents compliance evidence for each requirement, (c) identifies any gaps for remediation
Responsible (R): IT Security Manager
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 8–16 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1205_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1205_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1205_Task7" name="Gap remediation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Gap remediation: For any PCI-DSS gaps identified in Step 2 or previous audit: (a) IT Security Manager creates remediation plan with timeline and responsible team, (b) common gaps in retail environments: (i) POS terminal physical security, (ii) network segmentation weakness, (iii) weak passwords on POS systems, (iv) missing logging and monitoring, (v) insufficient penetration testing frequency, (c) implements fixes with Network Infrastructure Team and POS Vendor; documents remediation evidence
Responsible (R): IT Security Manager / Network Team
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Varies (20–40 hours typical)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1205_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1205_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1205_Task8" name="Quarterly vulnerability scans">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Quarterly vulnerability scans: Approved Scanning Vendor (ASV) conducts quarterly external vulnerability scans of CDE-facing systems: (a) scans internet-facing payment gateway integration endpoints, (b) identifies vulnerabilities (CVE-based), (c) classifies severity, (d) IT Security Manager remediates critical/high vulnerabilities within 30 days; evidence submitted to ASV for re-scan and passing report
Responsible (R): IT Security Manager / ASV
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1205_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1205_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1205_Task9" name="Annual QSA on-site audit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Annual QSA on-site audit: QSA conducts annual on-site audit (typically 3–5 days): (a) interviews IT Security Manager, network team, POS team, and store operations, (b) inspects POS terminals at sampled stores (typically 5–10 stores), (c) reviews network diagrams, firewall rules, access logs, and encryption configurations, (d) observes POS terminal physical security, (e) tests incident response procedures, (f) produces Report on Compliance (ROC) with findings
Responsible (R): QSA / IT Security Manager
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 40 hours (IT team) + 3–5 days QSA</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1205_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1205_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1205_Task10" name="Audit finding remediation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Audit finding remediation: For any findings from QSA audit: (a) IT Security Manager creates remediation plan with evidence collection timeline, (b) implements fixes and documents evidence, (c) submits evidence to QSA for follow-up validation, (d) obtains formal Attestation of Compliance (AOC) from QSA upon successful remediation, (e) submits AOC to acquiring bank and card brands
Responsible (R): IT Security Manager
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 10–20 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1205_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1205_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1205_Task11" name="Compliance monitoring and reporting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Compliance monitoring and reporting: IT Security Manager provides quarterly PCI-DSS compliance status to CIO: (a) scan results summary, (b) open remediation items and status, (c) upcoming audit schedule, (d) compliance costs (QSA fees, ASV fees, remediation costs), (e) risk assessment of any deferred remediation items; annual summary to CFO for budget planning
Responsible (R): IT Security Manager
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 2 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1205_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1205_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1205_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1205_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1205_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-324 (ensure controlled execution — Cybersecurity &amp; Privacy (PA-27.3).) | - operational: standardized POS image deployment, remote configuration management, and automated compliance checking; operational: POS software that encrypts all cached card data and auto-purges after sync
Owner: IT Security Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1205_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1205_Annotation13" targetRef="W1205_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
