    <bpmn:process id="W_W5523" name="W5523. Enterprise Pentest, Red/Purple-Team &amp; Attack-Surface Management Program" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual pentest-cycle planning; launch of a new internet-facing service or a major ERP/API release; critical exploited-in-the-wild CVE; or a high-severity external attack-surface finding
Frequency: Continuous ASM scanning; annual full-scope pentest &amp; purple-team exercise; per-launch targeted test
Volume: ~10–15 external-facing assets under ASM; annual pentest covers the ERP, API gateway (W257/W733), ecommerce &amp; mobile app (W395); ~60–100 findings/remediations/year
Owner: IT Security Manager
Participants: External pentest vendor (vetted per W4730), Application Manager, Head of Engineering, Network Engineers, Internal Audit, PCI QSA coordinator (W1205)
Source: workflow W5523 — Enterprise Pentest, Red/Purple-Team &amp; Attack-Surface Management Program</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5523_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5523_Lane1" name="IT Security Mgr">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5523_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5523_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5523_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5523_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5523_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5523_Lane2" name="Security Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5523_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5523_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5523_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5523_Start4" name="Annual pentest-cycle planning; launch of a new internet-facing service or a major ERP/API…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5523_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5523_Task5" name="Annual scope &amp; vendor engagement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Annual scope &amp; vendor engagement: Prioritize the internet-facing estate (ecommerce, mobile-app APIs per W395/VS-75, vendor portals, API gateway W257/W733, ERP internet surface); engage the accredited pentest vendor vetted per W4730
Responsible (R): IT Security Mgr
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 24 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5523_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5523_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5523_Task6" name="Continuous external attack-surface scanning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Continuous external attack-surface scanning: ASM tooling over the public asset inventory; new-asset detection on launch (the OT analog is the W5421 connected-device gate)
Responsible (R): Security Analyst
Accountable (A): IT Security Mgr
Duration: 1 hour/week triage</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5523_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5523_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5523_Task7" name="Pentest execution &amp; triage">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Pentest execution &amp; triage: Coordinate testing windows; validate findings; deduplicate against W367 vulnerability data
Responsible (R): IT Security Mgr / App Manager
Accountable (A): IT Security Mgr
Duration: 36 hours/year cycle</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5523_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5523_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5523_Task8" name="Remediation tracking &amp; retest">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Remediation tracking &amp; retest: Assign findings to owners; severity SLAs (Critical 7 days / High 30 days); verify via retest
Responsible (R): Security Analyst / App Manager
Accountable (A): IT Security Mgr
Duration: 40 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5523_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5523_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5523_Task9" name="Annual purple-team exercise">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Annual purple-team exercise: Scoped adversary emulation validating SOC detections (W367/W397) and IR runbooks (W383)
Responsible (R): IT Security Mgr / external vendor
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 24 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5523_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5523_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5523_Task10" name="Reporting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Reporting: CIO/Board metrics (findings MTTR, repeat-finding rate, ASM trend); pentest-evidence feed to the W1205 PCI QSA
Responsible (R): IT Security Mgr
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 8 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5523_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5523_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5523_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5523_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5523_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-324 (ensure controlled execution — Cybersecurity &amp; Privacy (PA-27.3).) | - operational: pentest vendors vetted via the W4730 TPRM attestation | - operational: findings tracked to verified retest under severity SLAs
Owner: IT Security Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5523_Assoc13" sourceRef="W5523_Annotation12" targetRef="W5523_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
