    <bpmn:process id="W_W5524" name="W5524. Enterprise DLP &amp; Insider-Risk Monitoring (Endpoint/Email/Cloud)" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: DLP policy-hit alert (endpoint/email/cloud); flagged separation of a privileged user (W152 T-0); insider-risk referral from VS-23/VS-159/HR; or the monthly policy-tuning review
Frequency: Continuous alerting; daily triage; monthly policy tuning; ~12 case investigations/year
Volume: ~2,500 endpoints; ~6,911 identities; ~40–60 triaged hits/month after tuning; ~10 flagged departure windows/year
Owner: IT Security Manager
Participants: Security Analyst, Data Protection Officer, HR, Legal, Loss Prevention Manager (VS-23), IT Infrastructure Manager (endpoint agents per W367 EDR)
Source: workflow W5524 — Enterprise DLP &amp; Insider-Risk Monitoring (Endpoint/Email/Cloud)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5524_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5524_Lane1" name="Security Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5524_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5524_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5524_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5524_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5524_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5524_Lane2" name="DPO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5524_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5524_Lane3" name="IT Security Mgr">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5524_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5524_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5524_Start5" name="DLP policy-hit alert (endpoint/email/cloud); flagged separation of a privileged user…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5524_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5524_Task6" name="DLP policy lifecycle &amp; tuning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: DLP policy lifecycle &amp; tuning: Maintain endpoint/email/cloud rules aligned to the data-classification standard (W709 governance council); monthly false-positive review correlated with W367 EDR telemetry
Responsible (R): Security Analyst
Accountable (A): IT Security Mgr
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5524_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5524_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5524_Task7" name="Alert triage &amp; disposition">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Alert triage &amp; disposition: Review tuned hits (~40–60/month) enriched with identity, device-compliance and departure status; disposition or escalate
Responsible (R): Security Analyst
Accountable (A): IT Security Mgr
Duration: 30 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5524_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5524_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5524_Task8" name="Departure-window monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Departure-window monitoring: Heightened monitoring for flagged separations in privileged roles (per W375/W152 T-0 revocation)
Responsible (R): Security Analyst
Accountable (A): IT Security Mgr
Duration: 1 hour/flagged case × ~10/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5524_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5524_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5524_Task9" name="Case investigation &amp; adjudication">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Case investigation &amp; adjudication: Confirmed-hit investigation with HR/Legal/Loss Prevention (VS-23); evidence handled under the VS-88 legal-hold chain-of-custody
Responsible (R): Security Analyst / HR / Legal
Accountable (A): IT Security Mgr
Duration: 6 hours/case × ~12/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5524_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5524_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5524_Task10" name="Privacy assurance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Privacy assurance: Review the employee-monitoring basis with the DPO — RA 10173 proportionality, notice and retention
Responsible (R): DPO / IT Security Mgr
Accountable (A): DPO
Duration: 4 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5524_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5524_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5524_Task11" name="Metrics &amp; reporting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Metrics &amp; reporting: Insider-risk KPIs to the CIO; case-outcome feed to the VS-159/VS-23 investigation programs
Responsible (R): IT Security Mgr
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 4 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5524_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5524_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5524_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5524_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5524_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-324 (ensure controlled execution — Cybersecurity &amp; Privacy (PA-27.3).) | - operational: the monitoring basis reviewed with the DPO under RA 10173 proportionality | - operational: case evidence managed under the VS-88 legal-hold chain-of-custody
Owner: IT Security Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
