    <bpmn:process id="W_W5558" name="W5558. Ransomware &amp; Destructive Cyber-Attack Enterprise Response Protocol" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Confirmed or strongly suspected enterprise-scale destructive cyber attack — simultaneous encryption, disabling, or data destruction across multiple production systems (ERP core, POS/SCO estate, ecommerce platform, WMS, or the corporate network) — with or without an extortion demand received
Frequency: Rare, high-impact: no chain-wide destructive event in BuildRight&#x27;s history; the class is exercised annually through the W1330 scenario rotation&#x27;s ransomware-on-ERP inject and refreshed per W390&#x27;s BIA cycle — readiness is exercised, not event-driven volume
Volume: 1 event × the blast radius (up to ~600 POS terminals + ~1,500 endpoints + the cloud estate per W383&#x27;s own census) × the trading surface (up to ~205 sites switched to manual trading mode) × the recovery stack (immutable backups W382, W55 failover, ring-by-ring rebuild)
Owner: CIO
Participants: IT Security Manager (W383 command), IT Infrastructure Lead (W55/W382), platform &amp; ERP teams, VP Store Operations &amp; Regional Managers (manual trading mode), Legal Counsel (VS-100 — extortion demand monopoly), Data Protection Officer (VS-91, W53 clock), Corporate Communications (W134/W855), Treasury (payment rails), Insurance Coordinator (VS-26 cyber policy), external IR/forensics retainer, PNP Anti-Cybercrime Group &amp; CERT-PH, card brands/acquirer (POS-data cases), Board Audit &amp; Risk Committee (VS-36), Internal Audit (VS-21)
Source: workflow W5558 — Ransomware &amp; Destructive Cyber-Attack Enterprise Response Protocol</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5558_LaneSet8">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5558_Lane1" name="IT Security Mgr">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5558_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5558_Task17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5558_Start9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5558_Lane2" name="CIO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5558_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5558_Lane3" name="Legal">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5558_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5558_Lane4" name="VP Store Operations">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5558_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5558_Lane5" name="External Retainer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5558_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5558_Lane6" name="IT Infrastructure Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5558_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5558_Lane7" name="Insurance Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5558_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5558_End18</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5558_Start9" name="Confirmed or strongly suspected enterprise-scale destructive cyber attack — simultaneous…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5558_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5558_Task10" name="Enterprise declaration &amp; isolation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Enterprise declaration &amp; isolation: IT Security declares the enterprise cyber-crisis on multi-system confirmation (perfection of scope is not required to declare); execute segmentation kill-switches on affected segments; isolate the DR environment before any failover (synchronous replication extends the blast radius — W55&#x27;s own risk register); preserve volatile evidence per W383.3
Responsible (R): IT Security Mgr / Infrastructure
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 1–3 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5558_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5558_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5558_Task11" name="Crisis command &amp; communications lockdown">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Crisis command &amp; communications lockdown: CIO chairs the cyber crisis bridge (the security-class analog of the W848 CMT); external comms embargo with a single spokesperson per W134/W855 — no technical detail leaves the bridge; all extortion correspondence routed to Legal, never answered by IT staff
Responsible (R): CIO / Corporate Communications
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: First 24 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5558_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5558_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5558_Task12" name="Extortion-demand handling">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Extortion-demand handling: Legal owns the demand: the default position is no payment; any consideration runs only through Board + external counsel with sanctions/victim-funds screening before decision; law-enforcement referral to PNP ACG (RA 10175) and CERT-PH within 24 hours; demand artifacts (wallet addresses, samples, leak-site URLs) preserved and shared through W397 CTI channels; any payment decision requires CFO + CEO dual authorization riding W320&#x27;s payment controls
Responsible (R): Legal / External Counsel
Accountable (A): CEO (Board-informed)
Duration: 24–72 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5558_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5558_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5558_Task13" name="Chain-wide manual trading mode">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Chain-wide manual trading mode: stores on offline POS floor-limit discipline per the W535/W5G rails with cash-tender emphasis; ecommerce intake suspended or degraded per the W659 incident rails; DCs on the W580-class paper operations; closure decisions ride the E-02 closure custody (W2510 decides, W850 executes), never store improvisation
Responsible (R): VP Store Operations / Regional Managers
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: First 24 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5558_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5558_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5558_Task14" name="Scoping, PII &amp; payment-data determination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Scoping, PII &amp; payment-data determination: external IR retainer engaged within 12 hours under the privileged direction of counsel; determine exfiltration vs encryption-only; PII touched → W53&#x27;s NPC 72-hour clock; POS card data → W1205&#x27;s PCI forensic investigator engagement and acquirer notification
Responsible (R): External Retainer / IT Security Mgr
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 2–5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5558_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5558_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5558_Task15" name="Clean rebuild &amp; staged restoration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Clean rebuild &amp; staged restoration: rebuild from immutable/air-gapped backup copies per W382; enterprise credential, secret, and certificate resets (W375/W377); the W5521 change freeze holds throughout; restore in W390&#x27;s BIA dependency order with integrity verification before each ring reopens to traffic
Responsible (R): IT Infrastructure Lead / Platform Teams
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 1–4 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5558_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5558_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5558_Task16" name="Financial, insurance &amp; disclosure chain">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Financial, insurance &amp; disclosure chain: cyber-policy notice filed within the policy window (VS-26); business-interruption and response-cost capture; statutory filings protected via the W5546-class filing contingency where portals or signing rails are unavailable; listed-company disclosure assessment per W5017/W5019 with Legal &amp; IR
Responsible (R): Insurance Coordinator / Legal / IR
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Parallel, ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5558_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5558_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5558_Task17" name="Post-incident &amp; retrofit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Post-incident &amp; retrofit: full timeline per W383.6 extended to a Board-level review; control retrofit and ISMS documentation update (W5522); lessons fed to W397 CTI; a tabletop re-run within 90 days
Responsible (R): IT Security Mgr
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 2–4 weeks post-recovery</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5558_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5558_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5558_End18" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5558_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5558_Annotation19">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-324 (ensure controlled execution — Cybersecurity &amp; Privacy (PA-27.3).) | - operational: no extortion contact outside Legal; dual authorization (W320 rails) on any ransom consideration; DR isolated before failover, evidenced in the runbook; NPC/card-brand notification clocks evaluated within 24 hours of declaration
Owner: CIO</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5558_Assoc20" sourceRef="W5558_Annotation19" targetRef="W5558_Start9" associationDirection="None" />
